  "body": "Found while working #3748.\n\n## What happens\n\nA new 2D Offset operation starts with \"Pass starts at\" Auto and the lead-in type Helix (`crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs`, `seed_offset2d`). When the user sets Inside or Outside, the entry stays Helix. After #3748 the operation then gives the warning `EntryNotRecommended` (\"the Helix entry is used as selected, but Arc is recommended ...\"), and the Lead in page shows the same text.\n\nThe maintainer's words on #3741: \"an outside cut would default to a ARC or straight approach in the plane of its cut\".\n\n## Why it is not in #3748\n\nThe seed is the default of every 2D Offset area, pockets and Auto included. A change to Arc reaches about 17 test files of the app and UI crates that create a 2D Offset without an entry. #3748 keeps its scope to the warning, the page text and the removal of the automatic ramp. See `docs/decisions/3748-entry-warnings.md`.\n\n## Workaround\n\nSelect Arc on the Lead in / Lead out page.\n\n## Done means\n\nA 2D Offset with \"Pass starts at\" Inside or Outside uses Arc unless the user selects another type, and no `EntryNotRecommended` warning shows for an operation that the user did not change. The choice of how (the seed, or a change of the entry when the start side changes, as one undoable command) is recorded in `docs/decisions/`.\n",
